<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6007" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιπίπτω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιπερι-πίτνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fall upon and embrace, embrace eagerly,</i> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλον πόσιν ἀμφιπεσοῦσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.523
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				15.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιπίτνουσα τὸ σὸν γόνυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					278
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτ᾽ ἀμφιπίπτων στόμασιν</span>
			<i>embracing</i> so as to kiss, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				938
			</span></i>; <i>fall over,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προβάτοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parth.
					8.4
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <i>take to one's heart,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθνος Λοκρῶν ἀμφέπεσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).98
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
